186432686 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432686 1071 "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nI. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z-1}}{{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432686 1072 #uuid "0d9f5142-140d-5b22-b957-299741979b12" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432686 1074 "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I matches the definition:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\n$$\n\n- Integral II matches the definition:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z-1}}{{e}^{t}}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\n$$\n\n- Integral III does *not* match the definition. The lower bound of integration does not match that given in the definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432687 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432682 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432687 1069 "q-107862" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432687 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432687 1071 "$Γ(\\frac{1}{2})+4\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432687 1072 #uuid "0fdfcf02-67ae-5263-baa1-a6ba5d9b1b6d" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432687 1074 "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=\\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2})=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi }=\\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nΓ(\\frac{1}{2})+4\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }+4\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }=4\\sqrt{\\pi }.\n$$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432688 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432681 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432688 1069 "q-107833" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432688 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432688 1071 "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nI. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{{t}^{z-1}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z-1}}{{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}t}{{t}^{1-z}{e}^{t}}$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432688 1072 #uuid "2346f7c5-c1ac-509c-ac43-d1a23908e3df" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432688 1074 "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I does *not* match the definition. The integrand $\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{t}^{z-1}}$ is not equivalent to that shown in the definition.\n\n- Integral II does *not* match the definition.  The lower bound of integration does not match that given in the definition.\n\n- Integral III matches the definition:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}t}{{t}^{1-z}{e}^{t}}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432689 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432680 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432689 1069 "q-107886" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432689 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432689 1071 "$Γ(\\frac{7}{2})+Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432689 1072 #uuid "38540fee-f0e4-596e-9eff-9715fa0a19af" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432689 1074 "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{7}{2}) & =\\frac{5}{2}\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\,Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nΓ(\\frac{7}{2})+Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{15}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }+\\sqrt{\\pi }=\\frac{23}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }.\n$$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432690 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432674 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432690 1069 "q-107829" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432690 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432690 1071 "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nI. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{{t}^{1-z}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432690 1072 #uuid "43b66f9d-fca5-54ae-b724-0bc204fa830b" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432690 1074 "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I matches the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{{t}^{1-z}}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Integral II does *not* match the definition. The lower bound of integration does not match that given in the definition.\n\n- Integral III does *not* match the definition. The integrand ${t}^{z-1}{e}^{t}$ is not equivalent to that shown in the definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432691 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432683 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432691 1069 "q-107848" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432691 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432691 1071 "Evaluate $Γ(3).$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432691 1072 #uuid "58e93e99-d92a-5ce1-a5e1-f2a7ff45e177" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432691 1074 "For any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(n)=(n-1)!.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nΓ(3)=2!=2.\n$$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432692 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432685 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432692 1069 "q-107855" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432692 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432692 1071 "Evaluate $4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2}).$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432692 1072 #uuid "6bbc8ec2-1cd6-5115-ab81-c2fbacd13746" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432692 1074 "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) & =\\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{\\pi }}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }=3\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432693 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432677 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432693 1069 "q-107832" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432693 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432693 1071 "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nI. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{t}^{z-1}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z}}{t{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432693 1072 #uuid "8aae46a7-7405-5484-9202-26c3555ea95d" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432693 1074 "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I does *not* match the definition. The integrand $\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{t}^{z-1}}$ is not equivalent to that shown in the definition.\n\n- Integral II matches the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z}}{t{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Integral III matches the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432694 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432676 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432694 1069 "q-107853" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432694 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432694 1071 "$Γ(45)=$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432694 1072 #uuid "8f3249d6-edac-5050-9528-d13b2bdbb793" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432694 1074 "For any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(n)=(n-1)!\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nΓ(45)=44!\n$$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432695 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432675 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432695 1069 "q-107860" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432695 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432695 1071 "Evaluate $\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\,Γ(\\frac{9}{2}).$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432695 1072 #uuid "bd01511b-f45a-5cd4-b173-d099f3266062" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432695 1074 "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\,Γ(\\frac{9}{2}) & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot Γ(\\frac{7}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\  & =7\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432696 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432673 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432696 1069 "q-107845" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432696 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432696 1071 "$Γ(27)=$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432696 1072 #uuid "cb5b08f1-b473-53d8-ae61-be733c058e2d" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432696 1074 "For any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(n)=(n-1)!\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nΓ(27)=26!\n$$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432697 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432678 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432697 1069 "q-107849" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432697 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432697 1071 "Evaluate $Γ(6).$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432697 1072 #uuid "d0d87553-dab1-5046-8598-8f79d15fc0d7" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432697 1074 "For any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(n)=(n-1)!.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nΓ(6)=5!=120.\n$$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432698 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432679 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432698 1069 "q-107838" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432698 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432698 1071 "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nI. $3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{3z-1}}{{e}^{{t}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nII. $3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3z-3}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nIII. $3{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{t}^{3z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432698 1072 #uuid "ef7933ca-459a-5897-8c5b-5b08b877b68b" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true] [17592186432698 1074 "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I matches the definition. We use a substitution $s={t}^{3},$ then $3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t=\\text{d}s.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3z-1}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3(z-1)+2}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3(z-1)}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}(3{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{s}^{z-1}{e}^{-s}\\,\\text{d}s=Γ(z).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Integral II does *not* match the definition. The integrand ${t}^{3z-3}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}$ is not equivalent to that shown in the definition.\n\n- Integral III does *not* match the definition. The lower bound of integration does not match that given in the definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534685 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-067a2195-d3de-5acc-b220-c39097febda2" 17592186432598 "answer-1162131c-43c4-54ff-92ec-db2b4f6a331a" 17592186432599 "answer-11aa345c-1d7a-5608-9304-b98b59643044" 17592186432600 "answer-1365d528-3559-5e8c-aab0-a5fb4cd1c0ed" 17592186432601 "answer-14bc919f-37b1-5bfd-9092-4f4fec1c9b34" 17592186432602 "answer-15b2ab14-edca-5f56-b447-4b5fab9c2703" 17592186432603 "answer-179d6519-3f5e-5e5c-931a-bef96f2e6027" 17592186432604 "answer-1856db13-851f-5360-910f-bf03676b767e" 17592186432605 "answer-192695b8-ba15-56d7-992c-59c67d9779c9" 17592186432606 "answer-272b993d-cfcd-5fbc-8438-b2fc2453c336" 17592186432607 "answer-2d9f6e2a-09b6-5d76-a955-98ec83b942b9" 17592186432608 "answer-31575386-b43c-5cfb-b9cf-056d4be6aa3e" 17592186432609 "answer-339fc1c0-3378-5749-a840-c336809f200e" 17592186432610 "answer-3517e5b4-f44f-5fdf-86dc-8c2764fac2fa" 17592186432611 "answer-3901ff5a-02a7-5f69-8b78-2dc0868c8386" 17592186432612 "answer-45349eef-8d3d-5379-9b8b-6f793b4003b9" 17592186432613 "answer-45dd61c6-4646-5510-9b63-d54bc159f05b" 17592186432614 "answer-461bf02a-0b0d-5764-8758-d03d9e57079c" 17592186432615 "answer-499ba395-f3f1-51bf-ae69-2598a54d8a85" 17592186432616 "answer-509a5a08-2a17-53d6-bfc0-859e810cfe28" 17592186432617 "answer-57f6601b-563c-5b31-a64c-7ec8c55ad32b" 17592186432618 "answer-5a3da224-1c13-581e-8e58-d2d8d7580f45" 17592186432619 "answer-5c4d0a3c-d3e6-501a-ae95-afa45890cb45" 17592186432620 "answer-5d513a95-f295-54c8-8a9c-aee17a71f839" 17592186432621 "answer-5fecaf9c-523b-5840-82f6-4a073fed5f55" 17592186432622 "answer-60a4904e-dcde-5ed0-889d-30606d3a21d2" 17592186432623 "answer-639720b8-fabf-54a8-9b8c-e26d7c484dd0" 17592186432624 "answer-680dd59f-269a-5239-be6c-db7639bc6aff" 17592186432625 "answer-6c60091c-6a50-58f6-8506-d0161e3cbf8a" 17592186432626 "answer-713dac32-c8df-56dd-8214-cb5f985996e7" 17592186432627 "answer-7b0f4d46-fb0d-5d75-9842-205230ceda38" 17592186432628 